{#-
  The shell every page of the site is built into. A page supplies its own <main> and nothing else:
  the doctype, the head, the stylesheet links, the header, the persona card, the persona sheet and
  the index of every world are written once, here.

  Front matter a page may set:
    title       the page's name, the same words every link to it uses (see _data/worlds.json):
                every page sets it, index.html included ("the threshold"), and " · interesting"
                is appended to it in the <title>.
    description the <meta name='description'>: one plain sentence a search result or a shared
                link shows, omitted when absent.
    stylesheet  a name in css/: "quiet-room" links css/quiet-room.css after the shared
                css/site.css, so the page's own rules win over the shared ones. Omit it for a page
                that needs none.
    inlineStyles
                write the styles into the page instead of linking them. Only error.html needs it:
                CloudFront returns that page for any 404, at whatever path was asked for, so a
                relative <link> next to it would be a guess.
    siteRoot    the site's root as a path, for the same page and the same reason: with it set
                to "/", every shared script and link is written from the root, so a visitor who
                lands on the 404 page at /some/deep/path still gets the scripts and can leave.
                It is the one place the site names where it is served from: "/" is right for
                makeitmoreinteresting.com, and a copy served under a sub-path sets that sub-path
                here instead ("/interesting/"). Every other page leaves it out and keeps
                relative links, so they work under any sub-path unchanged.

  A page sets nothing about navigation. The header, the persona card and the world index are the
  whole of the shared chrome, and they are the same on every page: a page that wants to offer
  something does it inside its own <main>, under its own heading.

  The shared chrome, top to bottom, and why it is this size:
    the header   the site's name, one line about it, and three links: the threshold, the mood
                 atlas, site map. Nothing else lives here; in particular no status line.
    the persona  the one thing a visitor configures here, shown the way a game shows its player:
                 a portrait of their sky, one line on where things stand, and one button that
                 opens the sheet (js/persona.js). With no persona yet the card is unlit and the
                 button beckons, so the first thing to do is the first thing seen. The mood flow
                 is visible here too: on the threshold the card asks one sideways question on
                 arrival, inline, and everywhere it says what was read and offers the one world
                 that reading opens onto. It sits outside <main>, so the question is never a
                 gate: every page is reachable with it ignored, skipped, or scripting switched off.
    the index    every world as a plain link, grouped, with the orientation each one answers to
                 (_includes/worlds.njk, from _data/worlds.json). Written once here, after <main>,
                 so index.html's own markup links every world and the reachability axiom holds
                 with scripting off. sitemap.html and moods.html list every page themselves, so
                 they are the two pages without it.
    the sheet    the persona's dialog, written after everything else and shown only when opened:
                 the constellation (stars placed, dragged and read) and the orientation (the
                 question, and what it read). Its headings come after the page's own, so the
                 heading outline a screen reader walks stays in order.

  Five shared lines in the <head>:
    js/analytics.js  the Google Analytics tag and the consent banner that gates it (see
                     ANALYTICS_TAG and check_analytics in .github/scripts/make_interesting.py).
    js/state.js      the one local-state document every page reads and writes through, and the
                     meta menu that exports it (STATE_TAG and check_state).
    js/persona.js    the persona: the sky every world under the sky reads, kept and changed in one
                     place, plus the card and the sheet above. Not deferred, so a page's own script
                     can read window.interestingPersona.stars() while the body is parsed.
    js/site.js       the shared helpers a page can call: window.interestingSite.unlock(), which
                     renders a part that needs a saved sky as powered down with the one button
                     that powers it (see the README, "Powered down, never broken"), and the
                     index's "send me somewhere" button. Not deferred either, and after the
                     persona it reads from.
    js/threshold.js  the mood flow's engine: the orientations, the library of query mechanisms,
                     the clock and time-zone signals and the partly-remembered reading. The persona
                     card and sheet are where it is seen (MOOD_TAG and check_mood).
  Three of them may never be dropped: a built page missing the analytics, state or mood line is
  refused. The files behind the first two are fixed; js/threshold.js is protected instead, so a
  run may rewrite the flow but never delete it. js/persona.js and js/site.js are ordinary site
  source.

  Links are relative, like every link in the site: it has no fixed domain and may be served under
  a sub-path, so "css/site.css" and not "/css/site.css".
-#}
{%- set here = (page.filePathStem | replace('/', '')) + '.html' if page else '' %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang='en' data-page='{{ here }}'{% if siteRoot %} data-root='{{ siteRoot }}'{% endif %}>
<head>
  <meta charset='utf-8'>
  <meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1'>
  <title>{% if title %}{{ title }} · {% endif %}interesting</title>
{%- if description %}
  <meta name='description' content='{{ description }}'>
{%- endif %}
{%- if inlineStyles %}
  <style>{{ 'site' | css | safe }}{{ stylesheet | css | safe }}</style>
{%- else %}
  <link rel='stylesheet' href='css/site.css'>
{%- if stylesheet %}
  <link rel='stylesheet' href='css/{{ stylesheet }}.css'>
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if siteRoot %}
  {#- The 404 page is served at any missing path, so its scripts are named from the site's root;
      see the note on siteRoot above. The five lines are the same five as below. -#}
  <script src='{{ siteRoot }}js/analytics.js' defer></script>
  <script src='{{ siteRoot }}js/state.js'></script>
  <script src='{{ siteRoot }}js/persona.js'></script>
  <script src='{{ siteRoot }}js/site.js'></script>
  <script src='{{ siteRoot }}js/threshold.js' defer></script>
{%- else %}
  <!-- Analytics and the cookie consent banner that gates it; see js/analytics.js. -->
  <script src='js/analytics.js' defer></script>
  <!-- The one local-state store every page reads and writes through, and its meta menu; see
       js/state.js. Not deferred: a page's own script runs before any deferred one does. -->
  <script src='js/state.js'></script>
  <!-- The persona: the sky every world under the sky reads, and the card and sheet it is set up
       in; see js/persona.js. Not deferred either, for the same reason, and after the store it
       writes through. -->
  <script src='js/persona.js'></script>
  <!-- The shared helpers; see js/site.js. After the persona, whose sky its unlock helper reads. -->
  <script src='js/site.js'></script>
  <!-- The mood flow's engine: ask before offering; see js/threshold.js. Deferred, and so after
       js/state.js, which is what it keeps its reading in. -->
  <script src='js/threshold.js' defer></script>
{%- endif %}
</head>
<body>
  <a class='skip-link' href='#main-content'>skip to main content</a>
  <header class='site-header'>
    <p class='site-header-title'>
      <a href='{{ siteRoot }}index.html'>interesting</a>
      <span>many worlds, no default</span>
    </p>
        <nav class='site-header-nav chips' aria-label='Site'>
{%- for link in worlds.wayIn %}
      <a href='{{ siteRoot }}{{ link.file }}'{% if here == link.file %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>{{ link.name }}</a>
{%- endfor %}
    </nav>
  </header>
  {#- The persona card: what a visitor with scripting switched off reads is written here and claims
      nothing; js/persona.js rewrites it, draws the portrait, asks on the threshold and un-hides
      the two controls. -#}
  <aside class='persona' id='persona' data-state='empty' data-sky='none' data-reading='none' data-asking='false' aria-label='Your persona: the sky you place and what this site has read about you'>
    <div class='persona-portrait' aria-hidden='true'><canvas id='persona-portrait' width='56' height='56'></canvas></div>
    <div class='persona-body'>
      <p class='persona-label'>persona</p>
      <p class='persona-text' id='persona-text'>No persona yet. Every world is on offer below.</p>
      <div class='controls persona-actions'>
        <button type='button' id='persona-open' aria-haspopup='dialog' aria-controls='persona-sheet' hidden>set up persona</button>
        <a class='action' id='persona-go' href='{{ siteRoot }}moods.html' hidden>go to your world</a>
      </div>
      <div class='persona-probe' id='persona-probe' hidden></div>
    </div>
  </aside>
  <div id='main-content' tabindex='-1'>{{ content | safe }}</div>
{%- if not (here == 'sitemap.html' or here == 'moods.html') %}
{% include 'worlds.njk' %}
{%- endif %}
  {#- The persona sheet: closed until the card opens it, and floating over the page when it does.
      Written last so its headings follow the page's own. -#}
  <dialog class='persona-sheet' id='persona-sheet' aria-labelledby='persona-sheet-title'>
    <div class='persona-sheet-head'>
      <h2 id='persona-sheet-title' class='panel-title'>your persona</h2>
      <button type='button' class='persona-close' id='persona-close'>close</button>
    </div>
    <p class='panel-note persona-sheet-intro'>A small sky of stars you place, and what the site has read of you. Every world reads from both, and both stay in this browser.</p>
    <section class='persona-section' aria-labelledby='persona-sky-title'>
      <h3 id='persona-sky-title' class='panel-label'>constellation</h3>
      <p class='panel-note'>Tap the sky to place a star, drag a star to move it, tap one to read its thought. The {{ worlds.underSky.length | words }} worlds under the sky read this one sky, each its own way.</p>
      <div class='persona-sky' id='persona-sky'><canvas class='persona-sky-canvas' aria-hidden='true'></canvas></div>
      <div class='controls'>
        <button id='persona-drop' type='button'>drop a star</button>
        <button id='persona-seed' type='button'>seed a small sky</button>
        <button id='persona-remove' type='button' hidden>remove this star</button>
        <button id='persona-clear' type='button'>clear the sky</button>
      </div>
      <p class='panel-status' id='persona-sky-status' aria-live='polite'></p>
    </section>
    <section class='persona-section' aria-labelledby='persona-reading-title'>
      <h3 id='persona-reading-title' class='panel-label'>orientation</h3>
      <p class='panel-status' id='persona-reading'></p>
      <div class='controls persona-reading-actions'>
        <button id='persona-ask' type='button'>ask me</button>
        <button id='persona-forget' type='button' hidden>forget my reading</button>
        <a class='action' id='persona-reading-go' href='{{ siteRoot }}moods.html' hidden>go to that world</a>
      </div>
      <div class='persona-probe' id='persona-sheet-probe' hidden></div>
      <p class='panel-note'>It never asks you to describe yourself, and it never asks the same way twice. <a href='{{ siteRoot }}moods.html'>The mood atlas</a> shows every way it asks and every answer it can arrive at.</p>
    </section>
  </dialog>
</body>
</html>
